                <head>Understanding between the United States and Canada regarding stationing of
                    naval vessels on the great lakes for the training of naval reserve
                    personnel</head>
                <p>[This Understanding, effected by an exchange of notes signed at Washington
                    November 18 and December 6, 1946, was based upon a new application and
                    interpretation of the Rush-Bagot Agreement of 1817. For text of Understanding,
                    see Department of State, Treaties and Other International Acts Series No. 1836,
                    or 61 Stat. (pt. 4) 4069.]</p>
            </div>
